// ---- Chapter 5: The little boy -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fifteen years ago a little boy gave a broken stranger an apple, bitten once "to see if it's a good one", the way
// the stranger's own daughter used to: Rowan, Sir Prince's son, and Lucian. Now Rowan is home and swears to hang The
// Fool. The guild holds back what it knows (a son will choose his father if the truth comes from a stranger). The
// Guard scribe who drew the Hale forgery, Oswin, names Varrick and his burned right hand, and is found hanged the next
// dawn with a fresh forgery and an apple stem under his feet. Through Nina, The Fool sends Rowan the Sun card, the
// page torn from Sir Prince's ledger (five children for "the north road", Nina first) and a music box. The case: the
// music box, recorded by the crystal, is a WAV whose right channel carries words drawn in the spectrogram above the
// tune: the old gallows, where the healer was hanged. Friday he will stand trial there, with Rowan as his judge.

